From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: margins on every monitor and a centred shelf

Maximized and tiled windows touched the screen edges on monitors without the
shelf, and on the shelf monitor's edges shared with another monitor, because
Mutter only honours struts on outer screen edges. The shelf now gives Mutter
its margin through meta_display_set_work_area_inset() (Mutter patch 0011).

A shelf sized to its content was centred by a width measured when an island
last changed; when the media or extras island appeared, hid or changed
width, the content sat off centre. The shelf now resizes whenever its
content no longer fills it.

--- a/js/ui/shelf.js
+++ b/js/ui/shelf.js
@@ -117,6 +117,15 @@
         const {children, sizes, gap, scale, length} = this._measure(container);
         const vertical = container._vertical;
         const available = vertical ? box.get_height() : box.get_width();
+        // A shelf sized to its content is centred by that size. When an island
+        // appears, hides or changes width without the shelf resizing, the old
+        // size no longer matches and the content sat off centre; ask again.
+        if (container._fitsContent && Math.abs(available - length) > 1 &&
+                container._askedFor !== available) {
+            // Once per size: a shelf clamped to its monitor stays shorter than its content.
+            container._askedFor = available;
+            container._lengthChanged?.();
+        }
         const gaps = shelfGaps(children, container._mediaIsland, container._statusIsland, gap,
             Math.max(0, available - length) / scale, container._liveIsland).map(value => value * scale);
         const rtl = !vertical && container.text_direction === Clutter.TextDirection.RTL;
@@ -486,6 +495,7 @@
